      "question": "If the sum of $n$ terms of an A.P. is $3n^2 + 5n$, find the $n^{th}$ term.",
      "finalAnswer": "$6n + 2$",
      "solutionSteps": [
        "$a_n = S_n - S_{n-1}$.",
        "$S_n = 3n^2+5n$. $S_{n-1} = 3(n-1)^2 + 5(n-1) = 3(n^2-2n+1) + 5n-5 = 3n^2-n-2$.",
        "$a_n = (3n^2+5n) - (3n^2-n-2) = 6n+2$."
      ]
